
 
1.	Sprint 1 Overview
Sprint 1 will discuss the fundamental features for emissions reporting, analytics, driver assignment, fuel logging and export features. Vehicle CRUD functionality, account/role management and authentication will be focused.

Sprint 1 Goal 
Allow users to log in and out of application and also allowing fleet managers to manage accounts of users, roles, and records of fleet vehicles.
Sprint 1 Scope
Priority	Story	Feature	Story Points	Approx. Effort
1	US1	User Login	5 SP	8 h
2	US2	User Logout	2 SP	2.5 h
3	US3	User & Role Management	5 SP	9.5 h
4	US4	Create Vehicle	5 SP	9 h
5	US5	Edit/Delete Vehicle	5 SP	7 h
	TOTAL		22 SP	36 h

Why are these user stories in Sprint 1
•	Authentication must exist before users can access role-specific features.
•	User accounts and roles must exist before drivers can be assigned vehicles.
•	Vehicles must exist before driver assignment or fuel logging can work.
•	Completing create, view/update and delete operations establishes the basic vehicle-management foundation.
•	Stories 6–14 depend on these core capabilities and therefore remain in the Product Backlog for later sprints.
 
