8. Sprint 1 Definition of Done
1.	All acceptance criteria for the story are satisfied.
2.	Required Java/JavaFX functionality is implemented.
3.	Appropriate object-oriented design is used.
4.	Input validation and error handling are implemented.
5.	Relevant automated/unit tests are written and pass.
6.	The feature works correctly with the integrated application.
7.	Code is committed to the team GitHub repository using the agreed branch workflow.
8.	Code is reviewed before integration where appropriate.
9.	The completed functionality can be demonstrated to the team and tutor.
9. Dependencies and Implementation Order
Recommended sequence: US1 Login → US2 Logout / US3 User & Role Management → US4 Create Vehicle → US5 Edit/Delete Vehicle.
After Sprint 1, the logical feature path is:
Users + Vehicles → Driver Assignment → Assigned Vehicle View → Fuel Logging → Fuel History → Efficiency/Cost Analytics → Fleet/Emissions Reports → CSV Export
