C. Code changes to implement during Sprint 1
Area	Sprint 1 Implementation
User domain	User.java plus a Role enum (DRIVER / FLEET_MANAGER or team-agreed names).
Authentication	Authentication service/interface for validating credentials and identifying the current role.
Login/Logout UI	JavaFX Login view/controller plus logout navigation/session clearing.
User management	Fleet-manager-only UI/controller for displaying, creating and deleting accounts.
Vehicle domain	Vehicle.java with ID, registration, make, model, fuel type and odometer fields.
Vehicle persistence	DAO/repository layer for create/read/update/delete. If the project uses SQLite, keep SQL/data access out of UI controllers.
Vehicle UI	Vehicle list plus add/edit/delete forms/controllers.
Validation	Duplicate registration validation, required-field validation and sensible odometer checks.
Tests	Unit tests for authentication, role restrictions, account management and vehicle CRUD; use temporary/test data rather than production data.

D. Suggested Git workflow
1.  Pull the latest team branch before starting a story.
2.  Create a feature branch for the story/feature.
3.  Write or update tests with the feature where practical.
4.  Make small, descriptive commits (for example: “Add credential validation tests”).
5.  Push the feature branch to GitHub.
6.  Open a pull request and have another team member review it if the team workflow uses PR reviews.
7.  Merge only when the feature satisfies its acceptance criteria and relevant tests pass.
8.  Move the corresponding Trello card through In Progress → Testing/Review → Done.

